# cp to /opt/aurum/.env  then  chmod 600 /opt/aurum/.env
# deploy/install.sh does both for you.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile: no `export`, no quotes, no inline comments on a
# value line. A quoted value is read WITH the quotes.

# ---- the analyst ---------------------------------------------------------
# ONLY NEEDED FOR --provider anthropic: (the default), which bills per token.
# A measured read is ~$0.63 at opus list, and the live path's 30-minute
# heartbeat runs 46-92 reads/day -- $640 to $1,280 a month. See RUNBOOK step 5.
#
# --provider claudecode:claude-opus-5 runs the same model through the Claude
# Code CLI against a Pro/Max subscription instead, and needs NO key here. If you
# use it, LEAVE THIS UNSET: a key present in the environment is how a desk meant
# to run on a subscription quietly runs up a metered bill. Preflight warns you,
# and the provider strips the key from the CLI's environment, but the clean
# configuration is simply not to set it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---- price feed ----------------------------------------------------------
# READ-ONLY token. Aurum is advisory and never places an order; a token with
# trade permissions grants an authority the desk has no code to use.
# Practice account is correct for the shadow launch.
OANDA_TOKEN=...
OANDA_ACCOUNT=101-004-xxxxxxx-001
OANDA_INSTRUMENT=XAU_USD
# practice | live   (practice unless you have a specific reason)
OANDA_ENV=practice

# ---- signal delivery -----------------------------------------------------
# THE BOT THAT SENDS YOU SIGNALS. These were previously absent from this file
# while run_desk.py's preflight required them, so a clean install passed the
# env stage and then failed preflight with nothing to point at.
#
# Two ways to supply them, checked in this order:
#   1. the files secrets/telegram_token and secrets/telegram_chat_id
#   2. these variables
#
# The FILES are preferred and are what install.sh creates: an environment
# variable is visible in `systemctl show`, in the journal on a crash, and to
# anything that can read /proc. A 0600 file owned by the service account is not.
# Set these only if you have a reason to prefer env over files.
#
# Get the token from @BotFather, message your bot once, then run
# deploy/telegram_setup.py — it discovers the chat id, writes both files and
# proves a message arrives. You do not need to read a getUpdates dump by hand.
#TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:AA...
#TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890

# ---- external signal collector (optional) --------------------------------
# ONLY needed by signals_capture.py, which is a separate service. The desk runs
# without these. api.telegram.org's API ID/hash are NOT the bot token above.
#
# Telethon authenticates as YOUR user and writes a *.session file that is a live
# credential. It stays in secrets/, is hard-ignored by git, and must never be
# committed or copied off the host.
TELEGRAM_API_ID=...
TELEGRAM_API_HASH=...
